<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Summon Water</h1>
<p>Sphere: Summoning Sphere
Class: Conjurer (guild level 24, up to 80%)
Mana: 20
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre><a cmd='#'>cast summon water</a>
tell elemental &lt;command&gt;
</pre>
<p>A column of water rises, and from it a small water elemental (level 35) 
emerges to serve you. It follows you, fights beside you when you are in a 
fight, and when your hit points drop below a third it tries to rescue you. 
You can give it orders with tell: to attack (tell elemental kill orc), to 
walk, to pick things up or drop them, and the like. It won't hurt another 
player unless both of you have signed the Book of Blood.
</p><p>It can only stay on this plane a short time: from about twenty seconds to 
two minutes or more, longer the better the casting. Then it vanishes in a 
puff of smoke, dropping whatever it carried. If it is killed first, it is 
gone too. Only one summoned creature serves you at a time: summon another, 
and one of them is sent away.
</p><p>You must be standing, not fighting. It is also found on scrolls.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
